{"slug":"largest-number","title":"Arrange Numbers to Form the Largest","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"medium","order":159,"tags":["sorting","strings","comparator"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"A custom order for sorting","body":["To glue numbers together into the biggest possible number you cannot sort them as numbers (9 should come before 34) nor as plain strings (`30` before `3` is wrong: `330` beats `303`). The right rule compares two numbers `x` and `y` by the two possible gluings: put `x` first if `x + y` is greater than `y + x` as strings.",{"code":"from functools import cmp_to_key\ndef order(x, y):\n    if x + y > y + x: return -1     # x goes first\n    if x + y < y + x: return 1\n    return 0\na.sort(key=cmp_to_key(order))"},"This comparison is consistent, so sorting works. If the biggest number starts with `0`, every number was 0 and the answer is just `0`."]},"statement":["Given `n` non-negative integers, arrange them in an order so that the number made by writing them one after another is as large as possible. Print that number."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`.","The second line has `n` non-negative integers (without leading zeros)."],"outputFormat":["Print the largest number as a string of digits."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","0 <= each number <= 10^9"],"examples":[{"input":"5\n3 30 34 5 9\n","output":"9534330\n","note":"The order 9 5 34 3 30 gives 9534330."}],"hints":["Treat the numbers as strings.","Put `x` before `y` when the text `x + y` is greater than `y + x`.","If the result starts with 0, print just 0."],"starter":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = input().split()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<string> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        String[] a = new String[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["`x` must come before `y` exactly when `x + y > y + x` as text. Sorting with this rule and joining gives the largest number."],"complexity":"Time O(n log n * L) for numbers of L digits, space O(n * L).","code":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = input().split()\n\nfrom functools import cmp_to_key\na.sort(key=cmp_to_key(lambda x, y: -1 if x + y > y + x else (1 if x + y < y + x else 0)))\nresult = \"\".join(a)\nprint(\"0\" if result[0] == \"0\" else result)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<string> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    sort(a.begin(), a.end(), [](const string& x, const string& y) { return x + y > y + x; });\n    string result;\n    for (const string& s : a) result += s;\n    cout << (result[0] == '0' ? \"0\" : result) << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        String[] a = new String[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.next();\n\n        Arrays.sort(a, (x, y) -> (y + x).compareTo(x + y));\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (String s : a) sb.append(s);\n        System.out.println(sb.charAt(0) == '0' ? \"0\" : sb.toString());\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"5\n3 30 34 5 9\n","output":"9534330\n"},{"input":"1\n0\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"3\n0 0 0\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"2\n10 2\n","output":"210\n"},{"input":"3\n121 12 120\n","output":"12121120\n"},{"input":"4\n824 8247 8 82\